    Ballot: c1a00007 yes on resource-safety-metric-amendment
    
    Constitution VII confirmed: the amended metric still defers on a measured
    quantity (unreclaimable memory) and imposes no ceiling once headroom is
    adequate. A memory-safety deferral, not a worker cap. The clerk exemption
    reduces restrictions (not a cap) and prevents the circular deadlock where
    the guard defers the very function that must fix it.
    Constitution IX: ordinary legislation; Constitution not amended.
    Non-blocking refinements: (a) total 'slab' includes reclaimable slabs —
    slab_unreclaimable is more precise, but over-counting errs toward safety;
    (b) §3 rationale still mentions 'page-cache contribution' although the
    metric no longer counts it.

